      "summaries": {
        "en": "Container is Apple's open-source tool for running Linux containers on Mac using lightweight VMs, optimized for Apple Silicon. It leverages the Virtualization framework to boot Linux kernels directly, achieving near-native performance without Docker Desktop's overhead. Developers can use it to test Linux software locally, build CI pipelines, or run server workloads on Mac hardware. Its Swift codebase makes it easy to integrate into macOS development workflows.",
        "zh": "Container 是苹果开源的 Mac 端 Linux 容器工具，专为 Apple Silicon 优化。它利用 macOS 的 Virtualization 框架直接启动 Linux 内核，以轻量级虚拟机方式运行容器，避免了 Docker Desktop 的资源开销，性能接近原生。技术亮点在于用 Swift 编写，深度集成 macOS 生态，开发者可轻松将其嵌入本地开发、CI 流水线或服务器负载测试。实际使用中，你只需一条命令就能拉起一个 Linux 容器，在 Mac 上无缝运行 Linux 软件，非常适合跨平台开发或快速验证 Linux 环境下的应用行为。",
        "es": "Container is Apple's open-source tool for running Linux containers on Mac using lightweight VMs, optimized for Apple Silicon. It leverages the Virtualization framework to boot Linux kernels directly, achieving near-native performance without Docker Desktop's overhead. Developers can use it to test Linux software locally, build CI pipelines, or run server workloads on Mac hardware. Its Swift codebase makes it easy to integrate into macOS development workflows.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "container gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Container is Apple's open-source tool for running Linux containers on Mac using lightweight VMs, optimized for Apple Silicon. It leverages the Virtualization framework to boot Linux kernels directly, achieving near-native performance without Docker Desktop's overhead. Developers can use it to test Linux software locally, build CI pipelines, or run server workloads on Mac hardware. Its Swift codebase makes it easy to integrate into macOS development workflows.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/apple/container for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
